  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe ring-link law reads `max_stay_down` on the pass link at `crates/motion/src/machining2d/ring_links.rs:118`. It does not read it on the planner join and the edge route at `crates/motion/src/machining2d/level_order.rs:264-269` and `ring_links.rs:158`.\n\nThus the edge route can stay down longer than the value the user set.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe limit is a user promise. The tool misses a lift that the parameter asks for. This is not a gouge: the review of #3818 proved each chord stays in the cutter-centre area.\n\nThe straight join has the same gap before this change.\n\n## Fix\n\nApply `max_stay_down` to each chord of the planner join and the edge route, in the same way as the pass link. Add a pin with a small `max_stay_down` and assert the lift.\n\n## Scope\n\nFound in the review of #3818 at head `968fa46d7`.\n",
